    "text": "We built a GTM bot on Claude Opus 5.5 this week, and I'm open sourcing it. \n\nPlug in the two tools from the video, open the folder in Claude Code, and it works your outbound from the buying signal to a written campaign.\n\nOn each run it:\n\n- Pulls fresh leads with the evidence attached, then checks your outreach history so anyone who already replied or opted out is left alone\n- Tiers each new lead A, B, C or DQ, and picks email, LinkedIn or both\n- Writes the sequence from the lead's data and your seller profile. A linter flags any % or \"2x\" claim that isn't one of your proof points\n- Sorts replies into ten types and drafts the answer... you still hit send\n- Rewrites its playbook from what came back, with a daily cap on how far its scoring weights can move\n\nAfter our first run, Opus called its 15 simulated outcomes \"not evidence\" and barely moved its signal weights.\n\nIt wants 30 real contacts per bucket before it trusts a result.\n\nIt's not perfect yet. Answering one test reply, Opus said pricing \"depends on seats and volume\", which isn't in our profile.\n\nSo read what it writes before you go live.\n\nNo model API key needed, it runs on your Claude Code login.\n\nYou get the code, the 5 Claude Code skills, the playbook, the linter and the send guard.\n\nFork it and rewrite the playbook for whatever you sell.\n\nThe article below walks through the whole build. Repo link in the replies.",
